# Technical Documentation: Drimo Web Ecosystem

Welcome to the **Drimo Web** technical reference guide! This document is designed to walk you through every folder, file, technical configuration, and industry-standard term used in this codebase.

Drimo Web is an **Enterprise Driver Human Resource Management System (HRMS)** built with a modern web stack. It supports multiple portals with different user privileges (internal administrators, driver support agents, drivers, and client organizations).

---

## 1. High-Level Architecture Overview

Drimo is structured as a single monorepo-style application that serves **three distinct user flows** using a single Next.js installation:
1. **Drimo Admin Portal (`/drimo`)**: For platform operations, payroll accountants, super admins, and support agents.
2. **Drimo Driver Portal (`/drimo/driver`)**: A mobile-optimized interface for drivers to log attendance, check support tickets, and see their payroll details.
3. **Client Organization Portal (`/org`)**: For clients (e.g., transport companies) using Drimo drivers. They can view attendance analytics, assign shifts, approve leave requests, and request driver replacements.

```mermaid
graph TD
    User([User request]) --> Mid[Next.js Middleware]
    Mid -->|Scope: 'drimo'| DrimoApp[/drimo pages]
    Mid -->|Role: 'driver'| DriverApp[/drimo/driver pages]
    Mid -->|Scope: 'org'| OrgApp[/org pages]
    
    DrimoApp --> API[API Endpoints /api/drimo]
    DriverApp --> API
    OrgApp --> OrgAPI[API Endpoints /api/org]
    
    API --> DB[(MongoDB Database)]
    OrgAPI --> DB
```

