#### 📂 `src/app/` (Pages & APIs Routing)
Next.js utilizes file-system routing. Inside this directory, folder names determine the browser path, and `page.js` or `route.js` determine what displays or runs.

- **`layout.js`**: Global wrapper that defines the HTML base tag, loads fonts (Inter from Google Fonts), and mounts globally available classes.
- **`globals.css`**: Styling foundation defining Tailwind imports, customized scrollbar overlays, core color CSS variables, and layout shells (such as `.drimo-shell` and `.org-shell`).
- **`page.js`**: The main project welcome landing page where users click to go to either the **Drimo Portal** or the **Organization Portal**.

- **📂 `api/` (Backend Endpoints)**
  - `📂 api/auth/drimo/route.js` & `api/auth/org/route.js`: Handlers for validating email/password, issuing JWTs, and storing cookies.
  - `📂 api/drimo/*`: Internal APIs (e.g., `/api/drimo/salary` processes payroll sheets, calculates monthly base pay minus absences, and issues batch IDs).
  - `📂 api/org/*`: Enterprise client APIs for fetching KPI scorecards, managing work shifts, and viewing attendance logs.

- **📂 `drimo/` (Admin Web Pages)**
  - `/drimo/dashboard`: Displays system-wide active stats (total drivers, active clients, unverified documents, open support tickets).
  - `/drimo/drivers`: Main driver database listing. Admins can create profiles, upload document metadata, change employment status, and link profiles to login accounts.
  - `/drimo/salary`: Payroll calculation worksheet. Calculates month-by-month attendance sheets, tracks half-days and leave offsets, and generates payout totals.
  - **📂 `drimo/driver/` (Driver Subportal)**:
    - `/drimo/driver/dashboard`: Driver homepage. Features a huge interactive **Punch In / Punch Out** button using geolocation details.
    - `/drimo/driver/attendance`: Displays the driver's own check-in/out logs calendar.

- **📂 `org/` (Client Web Pages)**
  - `/org/dashboard`: High-level metrics for HR managers (daily active headcount, today's absent count, active shifts).
  - `/org/shifts`: Scheduling calendar allowing supervisors to assign driver shifts.
  - `/org/kpi`: Metric score sheets that evaluate drivers based on late arrivals, customer feedback, and safe operation.
  - `/org/replacements`: Allows requesting immediate backup drivers in case an existing driver calls in sick or goes on leave.

