## 4. Summary Flow: How Everything Connects

Here is an example of what happens when a driver opens the Drimo App to **Punch In**:

```
[Driver UI] 
   └── 1. Clicks "PUNCH IN" (uses "use client" in src/app/drimo/driver/dashboard/page.js)
   └── 2. Browser grabs Geo-Location coordinates and snaps a verification selfie.
   └── 3. UI triggers a POST request to `/api/drimo/attendance`

[API Endpoint]
   └── 4. Middleware (src/middleware.js) intercepts request, reads cookie "drimo_token"
   └── 5. Verifies JWT (src/lib/auth/jwt.js) & extracts payload (driverId = X, scope = drimo)
   └── 6. Next.js router routes request to POST handler in api route
   └── 7. Handler imports dbConnect (src/lib/db/connect.js) to reuse database link
   └── 8. Mongoose maps input to Attendance schema (src/lib/db/models/Attendance.js)
   └── 9. Record is written to MongoDB!
   └── 10. Returns `apiSuccess()` (src/lib/helpers.js)

[Driver UI]
   └── 11. Sonner toast pops up showing "Punch In recorded successfully!"
```

This clean, decoupled architecture ensures that whether you are checking attendance, assigning shifts, or calculating a month's driver payroll, the codebase remains reliable, performant, and secure!
